== Geography ==

Tramuntana occupies the northern end of the Balboa isthmus, extending from the [[Shendan Ocean]] on the western coast to the borders of [[Nurra Province|Nurra]] and [[Tapuya]] on the east and north. The [[Yalabirga Mountain Range]] enters the province from the southeast, where it divides Tramuntana from Nurra, and runs northwest through the interior highlands before subsiding into the northern lowlands along the Tapuya border. The range forms the watershed divide: rivers on the western slope flow to the Shendan Ocean, while rivers on the eastern slope flow eastward into Nurra.

The province's topography is dominated by the Yalabirga highlands in the centre and south, with a coastal lowland along the Shendan coast to the west. The highland valleys, at elevations of 800 to 1,500 metres, support subsistence agriculture and livestock grazing, though the rain shadow climate limits crop production. The Shendan coastal plain is narrow and dry, lying in the rain shadow of the Yalabirga, with annual rainfall of 800–1,200 mm — conditions better suited to cattle ranching than to crop cultivation. The far northern comarcas, along the Tapuya border, are remote and sparsely populated, characterised by rugged terrain and extensive forest cover. The eastern comarcas, along the Nurra border, descend from the Yalabirga ridge toward the Aethiopian watershed but do not reach the Aethiopian coast.

The [[Gran Presa del Nord]], a major hydroelectric dam on a Yalabirga river in the eastern highlands, is one of the largest infrastructure projects in the province. It supplies electricity to Portblanc and the surrounding comarcas and feeds into the national grid.

[[File:Tramuntana savanna cattle ranch.png|thumb|right|300px|Cattle ranching on the Tramuntana savanna, the primary agricultural activity in the province.]]
