=== Climate ===

Tramuntana's climate varies with elevation and exposure, but the province is overall the driest in Balboa, lying in the rain shadow of the Yalabirga. The highland valleys experience a {{w|tropical highland climate}} with average annual temperatures of 18–24 °C, cooler than the coastal lowlands, but receive only 800–1,200 mm of rainfall annually — significantly less than the Aethiopian-facing slopes of the Yalabirga in Jala. The Shendan coastal plain is dry, with average temperatures of 26–29 °C and annual rainfall of 600–1,000 mm. The far northern highlands are the coolest and wettest part of the province, with the cloud forest zone receiving up to 2,500 mm annually, but this zone is limited in extent. The dry climate makes the province better suited to grazing than to crop production, and cattle ranching is the primary agricultural activity.

