The population distribution is highly uneven. The [[Cala Tranquilla (comarca)|Cala Tranquilla]] comarca, containing the provincial capital [[Portblanc]], accounts for approximately 44 per cent of the provincial population with a density of 653/km². The southern comarcas along the [[Expressway 1 (Balboa)|E1]] corridor — [[La Plana (comarca)|La Plana]], [[L'Horta (comarca)|L'Horta]], and [[La Conca (comarca)|La Conca]] — are the next most populous, with agricultural economies and rail connections to Sant Bart. The remote northern comarcas — [[Birú Nord (comarca)|Birú Nord]], [[El Pic del Nord (comarca)|El Pic del Nord]], and [[Els Cims (comarca)|Els Cims]] — are the most sparsely populated, with densities below 5/km².

== Demographics ==

With a population of approximately 1.9 million, Tramuntana is one of the least populous provinces in Balboa, containing approximately 5 per cent of the national population. The population density of 17/km² is the lowest of any Balboan province, reflecting the province's mountainous terrain and limited infrastructure.

The ethnic composition of Tramuntana reflects its history as a northern highland province. [[White Balboan people|White Balboans]] constitute the largest single group, concentrated in the highland valleys and the coastal towns. The white population is descended from Volisanian settlers and from the Illypnian immigrants who arrived under the [[Redilution]] and [[Birthing movement|Birthing]] programmes, which targeted the northern highlands. The proportion of White Balboans is higher than the national average, similar to the pattern in the Jala highlands.

The [[Birú people|indigenous Birú]] population, though small in absolute terms, is proportionally the highest in Balboa. The Birú are concentrated in the remote highland comarca of [[Birú Nord (comarca)|Birú Nord]], the largest comarca by area, where communities have persisted in relative isolation since the colonial period. The [[Birú Dale language]] is critically endangered, and the Birú community continues to face significant socioeconomic disadvantage.

[[File:Biru Nord highland community Tramuntana.png|thumb|right|300px|A Birú community in the remote highlands of Birú Nord.]]
